Look for bugs, missed requirements, shortcuts (skipped tests, suppressed warnings, swallowed errors), security problems (unsafe input handling, injection, secrets, unsafe defaults), and design problems worth fixing now: tangled responsibilities, needless coupling or abstraction, duplicated logic. Be concrete and brief.$(build_recheck "$1" "" "${2:-}")
Write the review to $RUN_DIR/review-$1.md and end that file with two lines: CODE REVIEW round $1, then VERDICT: APPROVE or VERDICT: REVISE
